Description: CVE-2026-107821 - insufficient validation of frm data when opening a table
 Upstream fix MDEV-40571 (commit 3b1c2e58abab5571bec4ff52773ddc75b1738da9)
 adds checks that the frm image is valid when opening a table. Debian
 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 (10.11.19) already ships that change in sql/table.cc,
 including the interval_nr > interval_count check, so the full upstream diff
 no longer applies (46 of 47 hunks are already present; the remaining one
 differs only in context). This patch carries the only piece still missing:
 the follow-up -Wmaybe-uninitialized fixup (upstream 23367c88), which
 initializes key_part_end in create_key_infos().
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/3b1c2e58abab5571bec4ff52773ddc75b1738da9
Author: Sergei Golubchik <serg@mariadb.org>
Last-Update: 2026-10-16
