Description: CVE-2026-107815 false positive — already in MariaDB 10.11.19
 Documentation-only note. Bookworm-security 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 already
 contains the MDEV-40637 cap in TYPVAL<double>::SetValue_char. The Debian
 tracker still lists this release as vulnerable.
Author: Root.io
Last-Update: 2026-10-15

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-107815.md
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE
+
+## CVE-2026-107815 — False positive on MariaDB 10.11.19 (Debian bookworm)
+
+### Overview
+
+CVE-2026-107815 is a buffer overflow in CONNECT `TYPVAL<double>::SetValue_char()`
+(MDEV-40637). A wide DOUBLE column could write the NUL terminator past a
+31-byte local buffer.
+
+### Why bookworm 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 does not need this patch
+
+The 10.11.19 orig tarball already contains upstream commit `b369925f`:
+
+    memcpy(buf, p, n= MY_MIN(n, 31));
+
+The MDEV-40637 regression test is already in `storage/connect/mysql-test/connect/t/fix.test`.
+Re-applying the os-patcher backport fails because that pre-fix context is gone.
+
+The Debian tracker still marks bookworm-security as vulnerable. That status
+has not caught up with the 10.11.19 source.
+
+### Verdict
+
+**No code patch required.** Treat scanner findings of CVE-2026-107815 on
+`mariadb` `1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1` as a **false positive**.
+
+This file is documentation only. It does not change MariaDB behavior.
+
+### References
+
+- https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107815
+- https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/b369925f6855d3e1f0ebcf453492724b99fda6f8
Description: CVE-2026-107823 false positive — already in MariaDB 10.11.19
 Documentation-only note. Bookworm-security 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 already
 stores view definer user and host as escaped strings (MDEV-40484). The
 Debian tracker still lists this release as vulnerable.
Author: Root.io
Last-Update: 2026-10-15

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-107823.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE
+
+## CVE-2026-107823 — False positive on MariaDB 10.11.19 (Debian bookworm)
+
+### Overview
+
+CVE-2026-107823 is view-definer spoofing in the `.frm` file (MDEV-40484).
+`definer_user` and `definer_host` were stored as raw strings, so a user name
+containing a newline could inject extra options such as `suid=1`.
+
+### Why bookworm 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 does not need this patch
+
+The 10.11.19 orig tarball already contains upstream commit `8a642bc8`.
+`sql/sql_view.cc` stores both fields as `FILE_OPTIONS_ESTRING`, and the
+MDEV-40484 regression test is already in `mysql-test/main/view_grant.test`.
+Re-applying the os-patcher backport fails because the pre-fix context is gone.
+
+The Debian tracker still marks bookworm-security as vulnerable. That status
+has not caught up with the 10.11.19 source.
+
+### Verdict
+
+**No code patch required.** Treat scanner findings of CVE-2026-107823 on
+`mariadb` `1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1` as a **false positive**.
+
+This file is documentation only. It does not change MariaDB behavior.
+
+### References
+
+- https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107823
+- https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/8a642bc8103aadc6b2087d781ba8e1595616a2c4
Description: CVE-2026-44169 - SHOW CREATE ROUTINE role privilege check (MDEV-39288)
 Upstream fix f279551013d1319f27344080e2c0758f3959cebf targets MariaDB 11.4
 where MDEV-29167 had refactored check_routine_level_acl() to take a
 privilege_t acl parameter; the role-branch incorrectly compared against
 SHOW_PROC_WITHOUT_DEFINITION_ACLS, masking SHOW CREATE PROCEDURE for users
 whose access comes from a granted role.
 .
 MariaDB 10.11.14 (this target) does NOT contain MDEV-29167. Its
 check_routine_level_acl() in sql/sql_acl.cc has no acl parameter, has no
 SHOW_PROC_WITHOUT_DEFINITION_ACLS symbol, and already uses SHOW_PROC_ACLS
 in BOTH the user-grant branch and the role-grant branch. That is exactly
 the post-fix semantic of the upstream patch, so 10.11 is not affected by
 this CVE on the source-code side.
 .
 To lock in this not-affected status and guard against future regressions,
 this patch back-ports only the upstream regression test (mysql-test/main/
 sp-security.{test,result}). The 11.x-only @save_sql_mode and conn1 hunks
 are dropped because the surrounding context does not exist in 10.11. The
 MDEV-39288 test block is appended after 10.11's existing
 "# End of 10.6 tests" marker rather than the 11.4 marker.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/f279551013d1319f27344080e2c0758f3959cebf
Bug: https://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-39288
Bug-Debian: https://github.com/MariaDB/server/security/advisories/GHSA-22xq-vq3f-87x2
Author: Sergei Golubchik <serg@mariadb.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-21

