Description: CVE-2026-107818 false positive — already in MariaDB 10.11.19
 Documentation-only note. Bookworm-security 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 already
 places the Galera wsrep bootstrap file under /run (MDEV-40629). The Debian
 tracker still lists this release as vulnerable.
Author: Root.io
Last-Update: 2026-10-15

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-107818.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE
+
+## CVE-2026-107818 — False positive on MariaDB 10.11.19 (Debian bookworm)
+
+### Overview
+
+CVE-2026-107818 is environment injection via the Galera wsrep bootstrap file
+(MDEV-40629). `mariadbd` could write the systemd `EnvironmentFile` because it
+lived in the socket directory, which the mysql user can write.
+
+### Why bookworm 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 does not need this patch
+
+The 10.11.19 orig tarball already contains upstream commit `e3d62d4e`.
+`support-files/mariadb.service.in` uses
+`EnvironmentFile=-@INSTALL_RUNDIR@/mariadb-wsrep-new-cluster`, and
+`scripts/galera_new_cluster.sh` writes that `/run` file. Re-applying the
+os-patcher backport fails because `INSTALL_RUNDATADIR` is already gone.
+
+The Debian tracker still marks bookworm-security as vulnerable. That status
+has not caught up with the 10.11.19 source.
+
+### Verdict
+
+**No code patch required.** Treat scanner findings of CVE-2026-107818 on
+`mariadb` `1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1` as a **false positive**.
+
+This file is documentation only. It does not change MariaDB behavior.
+
+### References
+
+- https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107818
+- https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/e3d62d4e78fd4941cef3f5053e6a50d0b32d740e
